# Review ownership.
#
# Requires "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection to have any
# effect. Without that setting these entries only auto-request reviewers; they
# do not block a merge.
#
# Last match wins, so the most specific rules go last.
#
# Both handles below resolve to real GitHub accounts, but CODEOWNERS silently
# ignores any entry naming a user without write access on this repo -- which
# fails open, leaving a path you believed was protected unprotected. Confirm
# write access, then check the repo's CODEOWNERS errors view after committing.

# Default: any change needs a maintainer.
*                               @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Skills and plugins: maintainer review.
/skills/                        @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/plugins/                       @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Contributor-facing process docs. Changing the review bar should itself be
# reviewed by the people who hold that bar.
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/MAINTAINING.md                 @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/README.md                      @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Automation runs with repository credentials. Any change here is
# security-sensitive and needs the security owner in addition to a maintainer.
#
# TODO: SECURITY_OWNER is unassigned. Until a real handle replaces it, these
# paths fall back to maintainer-only review -- which is the gap this section
# exists to close.
/.github/                       @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/.github/workflows/             @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/.github/scripts/               @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell

# Executable code shipped inside a skill. Reviewed line by line, by someone
# who owns that judgement.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS has no recursive-glob syntax that reliably matches
# 'scripts/' at any depth across all GitHub versions. The escalation labeler
# covers these paths by content instead -- see
# .github/workflows/route-review.yml. Do not rely on this line alone.
/skills/*/scripts/              @sfc-gh-chorgan @sfc-gh-lhartzell
